WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.975
Lab 2 runs the same inventory
against your own test tenant.

2
00:00:03.975 --> 00:00:07.417
You need a test tenant in
the worldwide or G C C cloud,

3
00:00:07.417 --> 00:00:11.925
with a test Azure subscription,
and a test Active Directory domain.

4
00:00:11.925 --> 00:00:14.650
Never production, and
only fictional people.

5
00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:18.125
Register a reading app with
a certificate, not a secret.

6
00:00:18.125 --> 00:00:22.376
Grant it Application dot Read dot
All and Directory dot Read dot All,

7
00:00:22.376 --> 00:00:24.425
and Reader on one resource group.

8
00:00:24.425 --> 00:00:25.994
Then run the inventory live,

9
00:00:25.994 --> 00:00:29.487
and compare the register with
the lists in the admin center.

10
00:00:29.487 --> 00:00:32.194
That comparison is what
tells you whether a real

11
00:00:32.194 --> 00:00:34.900
tenant returns the shapes
the fixtures assumed.

12
00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:39.590
To back it out, step eight removes the
Reader assignment and the two permissions,

13
00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:43.925
deletes the app registration and its
certificate, and deletes the output.

14
00:00:43.925 --> 00:00:46.075
The authors haven't run Lab 2.

15
00:00:46.075 --> 00:00:49.100
The workbook's Chapter 1
has the exact commands.
